/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   N9 local nav renderer — workspace-nav pattern ported from
   the Debs Boiler Plate mid version (horizon-2.0-alpha, nav.js
   + shell.css .sidenav rules), adapted to EAP content.

   Local to narrative-9-eap only — does NOT touch
   ../shared/nav.js, so N1–N8 and narrative-3-agile/2-pm are
   unaffected.

   Same external contract as shared/nav.js so call sites don't
   change:
     renderNav(activePage, { avatar, name, links, theme })
   links keys preserved from the old icon rail: 0=home, 2=setup,
   3=board — only the internal rendering changed.

   Rebuilt to match references/design-learnings.md §1 Left Rail
   (Debs Boiler Plate mid version) structurally, after the first
   pass wrongly simplified it. Per design-learnings.md: "The
   two-section structure (Menus + Your work) and quick-action
   strip are fixed" — universal chrome, not AICT-specific, so
   this version keeps them rather than omitting them:
   - Header: hamburger (toggles both ways) + logo + dedicated
     collapse button (one-way, hides itself once collapsed;
     re-expand happens via the hamburger — matches the source's
     two-control pattern, not a single merged toggle).
   - Quick-action strip: Home/Bell/AI-sparkle/Search/More —
     decorative global actions, inert, sits between logo and Menus.
   - Menus section: All/Favorites/History/Workspaces — present,
     inert (no EAP-specific target exists for these platform
     features yet; same "present but unwired" precedent already
     used elsewhere in this file for Notifications/Otto icon).
   - Your work section: workspace badge (EA / Enterprise Agile
     Planning) + EAP sub-nav (Home/Board/Setup) — the only
     functional items, wired via the links map exactly as before.
   - Icon glyphs for all chrome (menu, collapse, quickstrip, Menus
     items, gear) are the *exact* paths from the mid boilerplate's
     assets/js/icons.js registry, not reinvented.
   - Active-state fill: rounded-rect (~8px), dark charcoal via
     var(--color-primary) — per design-learnings.md §14 rule 1,
     never a full pill.
   - Deviation flagged: mid version doesn't do an outline/filled
     icon swap on active state (relies on bg colour alone) — this
     conflicts with this project's own established convention
     (outline default, filled on select). Priority given to source
     fidelity this pass; revisit if the project convention should
     win instead.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

